    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d558">

                <pb facs="0774" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1776: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-13T03:00:00+02:35">October 13, 1935—3
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. My 126, October 12, 5 p.m. Another special train was provided for the
                    Italian Minister at 10 o’clock this morning but again he refused to go.</p>
                <p>I am reliably informed that Vinci had a nervous breakdown and threatened to
                    commit suicide. He is reported to have said that he felt largely responsible for
                    the apparent failure of Italy’s policy in Ethiopia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
